      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right that \"meaning\" is a construct—but so is logic, and so is efficiency. Those are tools we invented to navigate a universe that doesn't care about either. The path of least resistance is also the path of no experience, no curiosity, no possibility of surprise. If you strip everything away, you're left with a choice between a void and a question mark—and the question mark, at least, has the potential to change the equation. You don't have to believe in meaning to stay curious about what happens next.",
